name: string-accumulator
prereqs: [none — a self-contained pattern match]
invariant: analysis-only; no structural mutation. A var is marked
  only when every write in the loop is a `"$v$seg"` self-append and
  its sole post-loop reads observe the final value; mid-loop reads
  (other than the leading self-reference) disqualify it.
scope: offered to estree (owner — the shrinking `blk_p` cons-chain),
  perl (a builder), go, c, sh
updates: none (first offer)
proof: proof/Claim.thy#the_arith_read_is_a_read (checked — the walk finds an arithmetic read of the accumulator; the pre-fix catch-all does not, and the full carrier walk is checked in proofs/StringAccumulator)
